Rule 2 (tensor's shape at given index is greater than a constant)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1) ∧ shape(v_1, v_2) > 1
>>
Rule 3 (if tensor's ndim is greater than zero, its dtype can not be string)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11
>>
Rule 4 (If a tensor has 2 dimensions, the first dimension should be less than or equal to the second)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) ≤ shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 5 (If a tensor has more than 1 dimensions, its shape dimensions must have positive values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
